{
  "repo": "EH3D-NODE-PNP-HEAD",
  "ecosystem": "eh3d",
  "tagline": "The node of the head of a pick-and-place machine: vacuum, puff of air, axes, lights, interlocks, two kinds of sensor.",
  "description": "EH3D-NODE-PNP-HEAD is the logic of the node that stands between the server and the head of a pick-and-place machine. The server asks over HTTP with a token; the node runs the pump, the valves, the axes and the lights under interlocks, senses the vacuum of each nozzle with a pressure sensor or a vacuum switch, tells a part held from a part lost, says when the machine may move in X and Y, and goes to a safe state by itself when the server is lost. All of it is tried against a simulator; the firmware and the hardware are not written.",
